@startuml
title Existing scheduler owns multi-agent execution
actor Operator
participant Controller
participant "AEO-3 Scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "AEO-2 Codex" as Codex
participant "Developer" as Dev
participant "Independent QA / Security" as QA
database SQLite
Controller -> Scheduler: prepare approved dependency-aware plan
Scheduler -> SQLite: verify plan, design, grants and leases
Controller -> SQLite: reserve run budget and intent
Controller -> Scheduler: dispatch bounded ready tasks
par Independent repository A
 Scheduler -> Codex: exact isolated execution A
 Codex -> Dev: structured task and context
 Dev --> Codex: artifacts and test evidence
else Independent repository B
 Scheduler -> Codex: exact isolated execution B
 Codex -> Dev: structured task and context
 Dev --> Codex: artifacts and test evidence
end
Scheduler -> SQLite: child results and handoffs
Controller -> QA: invoke AEO-4 independent validators
QA --> Controller: verified gates or bounded repair classification
Controller -> SQLite: observed outcome and audit
Controller --> Operator: report / exact pending authority
@enduml
